**Step 1: re-measure the BLUF and print each** (PR head and checks; alerts 12 and 13 with `path`, `start_line`, `tool.version`; the 11 python file names from `pulls/181/files`; `awk NR` of `deploy-from-ci.sh:117-120` and `test_deploy_pre1.py:463-468`, `:500-506`; the query file with `diff` against the tag copy; the csharp analysis and check timestamps). Write the emulator below to `.tools/b1521/scratch/emulate.py` and run it over the 11 files: **print `calls N flagged n`** (expected 6 and 2). Controls: it must flag exactly lines 468 and 506 of the branch head's test file, and the planted `0o750`, `0o710`, `0o644`, `os.open(.., 0o602)` while passing a planted `0o700` (a plant file in `scratch/`). **Any difference from this kit: write `MOVED`/`DIFFERS`, and STOP if it changes the shape.**

```python
# emulate.py <files...>: py/overly-permissive-file (codeql-cli/v2.27.4): os.chmod arg 1 or os.open arg 2 that is an integer
# LITERAL (or a name bound once to one in the same file) whose group or world digit is not zero.
import ast, sys
def perm(p):
    acc = lambda x: "writable" if x % 4 >= 2 else ("readable" if x != 0 else None)
    w, g = p % 8, (p // 8) % 8
    return ("world " + acc(w)) if acc(w) else (("group " + acc(g)) if w == 0 and acc(g) else None)
calls = flagged = 0
for path in sys.argv[1:]:
    tree = ast.parse(open(path, encoding="utf-8").read())
    bound = {}
    for n in ast.walk(tree):
        if isinstance(n, ast.Assign) and isinstance(n.value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(n.value.value, int):
            for t in n.targets:
                if isinstance(t, ast.Name): bound.setdefault(t.id, []).append(n.value.value)
    for n in ast.walk(tree):
        f = getattr(n, "func", None)
        if not (isinstance(n, ast.Call) and isinstance(f, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(f.value, ast.Name)
                and f.value.id == "os" and f.attr in ("chmod", "open")): continue
        i = 1 if f.attr == "chmod" else 2
        a = n.args[i] if len(n.args) > i else next((k.value for k in n.keywords if k.arg == "mode"), None)
        v = a.value if isinstance(a, ast.Constant) and isinstance(a.value, int) else (
            bound[a.id][0] if isinstance(a, ast.Name) and len(bound.get(a.id, [])) == 1 else None)
        p = perm(v) if v is not None else None
        calls += 1; flagged += bool(p)
        print("%s:%d os.%s %s %s" % (path, n.lineno, f.attr, oct(v) if v is not None else "non-literal", ("FLAG " + p) if p else "-"))
print("calls %d flagged %d" % (calls, flagged))
```

