At most TWO heavy jobs machine-wide across all MPS lanes. A heavy job here: each whole python-job loop (baseline once, head once). Take a slot by atomic `mkdir '<project>/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`), run ONE job, MOVE the holder file to `.tools/b1521/logs/`, `rmdir` your own dir; never touch another seat's holder (a holder older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed). **At drafting `.tools/.heavy-lock-1` existed (holder written 20:59) and `.heavy-lock-2` did not** (`ls -d`, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER; load1 12.68 at 20:56). Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (not independent: say so). Single-file runs, plants and the emulator are light. A wait is not a finding; at the hard stop `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`. Moved branch head or moved main: as Step 0 and Step 6.

